{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"935409ff47bd1aeb50b8a6736800bc1a55208b0c444d6913c1419208531f074b","digest":{"component_or_area":"file lock acquisition (_acquire_fcntl)","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/lock.py","_acquire_fcntl","acquire","fcntl.flock","LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB","EAGAIN","EACCES","ENOLCK","EIO","EBADF","tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py"],"problem_keywords":["error masking","errno discrimination","file lock","contention vs fault","timeout semantics"],"propositions":["_acquire_fcntl catches all OSError from fcntl.flock identically, masking genuine system faults (ENOLCK/EIO/EBADF) as spurious LockTimeout instead of propagating them with their errno.","EAGAIN and EACCES indicate lock contention and should retry until deadline then return -1; other errnos indicate genuine faults and should be re-raised immediately.","The file descriptor opened in _acquire_fcntl is not closed on all failure paths (timeout and re-raise), causing potential fd leaks.","All 12 callers of _acquire_fcntl handle LockTimeout as contention; branching on errno preserves contention behavior while fixing the fault masking bug."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785824746380670353,"uuid":"7be52c8b-a8fa-48f8-98b9-a14091a7a14c"}